# Git for Windows converts line endings on checkout by default, which is fine
# for source but not for a file this repository compares byte for byte. Pinning
# the working tree to LF everywhere keeps a Windows clone identical to a Linux
# one, and keeps the diff of a file edited on either the change that was made.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured verbatim from other programs and compared against what we write, so
# nothing may rewrite them -- not the committed bytes, not a checkout. Marking
# them binary is what says that, whatever a clone is configured to do.
*.acf -text
*.bin -text
*.txtpb -text
